@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `ydhX`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.06 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns.** Columns 1 to 79 are carried by 63 to 87%, 74 persistent and 5 shell, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 6% of calls {S2}. A branch of 58 families runs through columns 1 to 58, a parallel path carried in 11 to 13% {S2.b1}. The `rsxE` to `rsxA` genes, columns 38 to 43, are [[electron transport]] {S2.c38-43, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99 against 95%, and hesitates less there, 0.06 against 0.18 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 17, `lhr`, is a fork column, at 0.53 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Column 79, `ynfL`, is carried by 68% of chromosomes {S2.c79, E}. A branch of 3 families runs through columns 67 to 69, carried in 10% {S2.b67}.

@whole **Across the window it names 95% of genes**, 0.18 bits on average, perplexity 1.3 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 2.18 against 0.14 bits, and names fewer genes, 37% against 96% {C}.

